The stones is a list of 3, 2, 4, and 1.
The prefix is a list of 5 zeros.
For every spot from 0 to 3.
Set item (spot plus 1) of prefix to item spot of prefix plus item spot of stones.

The table is a list of 16 zeros.
For every length from 2 to 4.
For every start from 0 to 4 minus length.
The finish is start plus length minus 1.
The cell is start times 4 plus finish.
The before is item start of prefix, while the after is item (finish plus 1) of prefix.
The range is after minus before.
Set item cell of table to 1000000.
For every split from start to finish minus 1.
The beyond is split plus 1.
The leftcell is start times 4 plus split.
The rightcell is beyond times 4 plus finish.
The candidate is item leftcell of table plus item rightcell of table plus range.
If candidate is less than item cell of table, set item cell of table to candidate.

Show item 3 of table.
